Package: weightedMotifAccess
Title: Differential Motif Accessibility Analysis
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiayi", "Wang", email = "jiayi.wang2@uzh.ch", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Emanuel", "Sonder", role = "aut"),
    person("Pierre-Luc", "Germain", role = "aut",
           email="pierre-luc.germain@hest.ethz.ch", comment=c(ORCID="0000-0003-3418-4218"))
  )
Description: Provides tools for quantifying chromatin accessibility at
    transcription factor motifs from ATAC-seq data, with a focus on
    correcting for fragment-length and GC-content biases through fragment-
    and peak-level weighting. It further enables the discovery and
    characterization of interactions between pairs of motifs, testing whether
    the accessibility response at co-occurring motif pairs differs from that
    at either motif alone, and how this depends on the distance between the
    motifs. The package builds on betterChromVAR for computing bias-corrected
    motif accessibility deviations, and integrates with standard Bioconductor
    classes (GRanges, SummarizedExperiment) throughout.
